\f0\b \cf0 True Complementary Colors
\f1\b0 \
\
In the HLS color model, true complementary colors are found directly opposite each other on the hue circle (180 degrees apart). These complementary pairs create maximum contrast when placed side by side.\
\
Some key properties of true complementary colors:\
\
1. When mixed in equal amounts, true complementary colors produce a neutral gray\
\
2. They enhance each other's vibrancy when placed adjacent to one another\
\
3. They create a natural balance in color compositions\
\
\

\f0\b Working with the HLS Hue Circle
\f1\b0 \
\
The HLS hue circle is divided into 360 degrees, with the following key positions:\
\
- 0/360\'c2\'b0 = Red\
- 60\'c2\'b0 = Yellow\
- 120\'c2\'b0 = Green\
- 180\'c2\'b0 = Cyan\
- 240\'c2\'b0 = Blue\
- 300\'c2\'b0 = Magenta\
\
To find a true complement of any color, simply add or subtract 180\'c2\'b0 from its hue value.\
\
This system provides a reliable way to create harmonious color schemes with strong visual impact.\
\
\
